# Go tooling (gofmt, the CI gofmt check) expects LF. On Windows checkouts
# autocrlf would otherwise leave CRLF in the working tree, which makes local
# `gofmt -l` flag every file and hides real formatting drift. Pin Go sources
# (and other text the toolchain reads) to LF in the working tree too.
*.go text eol=lf
go.mod text eol=lf
go.sum text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for the SPA, one step further: CI diffs the committed embed
# (internal/api/ui/index.html) against a fresh Linux build, so the bundle has
# to be byte-reproducible across platforms. It wasn't. plugin/index.html was
# stored CRLF, and on Linux vite passed those template lines through verbatim
# while rollup emitted the inlined JS with LF, so the result matched neither a
# Windows-built embed nor itself across machines. Pin both ends to LF.
*.html text eol=lf
